  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rSite Location Plan P105; P100, P101, P102, P103, P104, Design & Access Statement, Flood Risk Assessment, Heritage Statement.\r\rReason: To ensure the development proceeds in accordance with the approved plans.",
    "Sound Insulation shall be provided as follows: \rA. In the form of either a floating floor or independent ceiling between the separating floors of the premises, as well as, to any internal walls that separate proposed individual dwellings from others and to walls that separate dwellings from any parts of the building that will be in common use (e.g. hallways, staircases and toilets) in order to achieve a level of sound insulation that, as a minimum, would meet the standard specified in Approved Document E: Resistance to the Passage of Sound (2003 Edition incorporating 2004, 2010, 2013 and 2015 Amendments); and \r\rB. For bedrooms and living rooms within the development in order achieve a level of sound insulation that would meet the 'good' standard for acoustic design criteria prescribed in British Standards Institute BS8233:2014 - Guidance on Sound Insulation and Noise Reduction for Buildings. The Sound Insulation to be provided shall be installed prior to the first occupation of the approved development and, thereafter, maintained as such for the life of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that the amenity of occupiers of the development is not adversely affected by noise from adjoining dwellings and communal space.\r"
  ],
